    "reason": "Arms every clip table as a selection, and lets a stride reach the two clips that ARE a subject's locomotion. The breeze whirls because Breeze.tick starts idle unconditionally, so its references were the frame vanilla draws only before a first tick: animation 0.1317 -> 0.0061. Its walk row carries that plus the slide, and the slide exposed a dropped channel - ClipKit knew the container under one spelling where the mesh had flattened a named part - which is 82.3441 unfixed and 0.0087 with it landing. The rabbit hops under a stride, having no walk-gated clip at all, and its walk row moves 0.0529 -> 0.0794 measuring an animal in motion rather than one held still. The pose table's two declared-rest keys were ordered by a Map.of salt that flapped per JVM launch and are now insertion-ordered, verified over three separate launches.",
